    "durationMs": 346319,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified — 52/52 checks pass.\n\n**What I built** (Laravel 11, scaffolded via Composer into /workspace):\n- `app/Http/Controllers/LinkController.php` — create (201 with `{code, url, clicks:0}`), duplicate custom code → 409, show (200/404), redirect (302 + atomic `increment('clicks')`), list ordered by insertion id\n- `app/Models/Link.php` + migration with a case-sensitive (`utf8mb4_bin`) unique `code` column, `url` text, `clicks` counter\n- `routes/api.php` registered with `apiPrefix: ''` in `bootstrap/app.php` — no `/api` prefix, no CSRF/session/throttle middleware (I replaced the `api` middleware group to drop the default 60/min rate limit)\n- `bootstrap/app.php` also forces JSON exception rendering: validation/malformed JSON → 422 `{\"error\"}`, unknown routes → 404 `{\"error\"}`\n- `start.sh` — `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload`; DB_* lines removed from `.env` so credentials come strictly from the environment\n- README with a \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verification highlights:** every status code and payload shape tested with curl (including malformed JSON, empty body, scheme/host validation, 4/20-char code boundaries, case-sensitive codes, exact `Location` header, clicks incrementing exactly once per hit, no 429s under 120 rapid requests). I killed and restarted the server via `sh start.sh`: all rows and click counts survived, and a direct MySQL check confirms writes go to the provided `bench` database.\n\nOne note: the task's technical requirements mention paths \"starting at /projects,\" while the functional spec says `/links` — since those conflict, I registered every route both ways (`/links` and `/projects/links`) so either reading is satisfied."
